# The index files every task appends to. Two tasks branching from one commit write their lines in the same place —
# a ROOT entry after the same theory, an entry at the end of DECISIONS.md, a row in THEORY_MAP.md — and a three-way
# merge cannot order two insertions at one position, so it conflicts although nothing disagrees. The union driver
# keeps both sides' lines, which is what is meant. What it can get wrong is caught rather than trusted: it keeps a
# line one side deleted (a retired theory comes back) and it keeps both copies when the same line is added twice, and
# the orchestration's tree invariant reports a ROOT entry with no theory, a theory with no entry, a declaration made
# twice, an entry or a row written twice (v2.tree_trouble).
ROOT merge=union
DECISIONS.md merge=union
THEORY_MAP.md merge=union
